    "text": "{\n  \"semantic_type\": \"dimension\",\n  \"unit\": null,\n  \"additive_over_entities\": null,\n  \"additive_over_time\": null,\n  \"time_rollup\": null,\n  \"valid_methods\": [],\n  \"period_basis\": null,\n  \"derivation\": \"Normalized label mapped from the XBRL concept in the SEC companyfacts feed, for example diluted_eps from EarningsPerShareDiluted, revenue from Revenues, and total_assets from Assets.\",\n  \"calendar\": null,\n  \"seasonal_adjustment\": null,\n  \"annualized\": null,\n  \"entity_grain\": null,\n  \"hierarchy\": null,\n  \"comparability\": null,\n  \"lineage\": {\n    \"source\": \"SEC EDGAR XBRL companyfacts API\",\n    \"url_template\": \"https://data.sec.gov/api/xbrl/companyfacts/CIK{cik}.json\",\n    \"retrieved_on\": \"2026-10-24\"\n  },\n  \"description\": \"Categorical label that says which financial statement measure each row's value holds. There are 7 distinct values: capex, diluted_eps, net_income, op_cash_flow, operating_income, revenue and total_assets. Use it only to filter or group rows, never to aggregate. The measures differ in kind and unit. Revenue, income, cash flow and capex are USD flows over a period. total_assets is a USD balance at an instant. diluted_eps is USD per share. Rows for different metrics must not be summed together, and the unit and period_basis columns should be checked within each metric. The underlying XBRL concept can differ by company for the same metric. For example, DRI's op_cash_flow uses a continuing-operations variant concept. Rows can also be quarterly, year-to-date or full-year.\"\n}",
